<title>USA: U.S. requires divestiture in U S West deal.</title>
<headline>U.S. requires divestiture in U S West deal.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Justice Department said Tuesday it would allow U S West Inc to acquire Continental Cablevision Inc as long as U S West divests Continental's interest in Teleport Communications Group Inc.</p>
<p>The department said the $11.8 billion merger, as originally structured, would have substantially lessened competition in certain markets for telephone services.</p>
</text>
